WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.755
An AI can suggest a fix in seconds.

00:00:02.755 --> 00:00:13.147
But who reproduced the bug? Which code was tested? And did the fix really work? PatchRoom brings those answers into one Switch room.

00:00:13.147 --> 00:00:18.500
This film presents archived evidence from an actual three-agent run.

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.988
A triager reproduces the issue.

00:00:20.988 --> 00:00:24.197
An engineer authors a minimal candidate.

00:00:24.197 --> 00:00:27.647
A verifier independently checks the result.

00:00:27.647 --> 00:00:31.499
Switch connects their conversation and handoffs.

00:00:31.499 --> 00:00:39.121
PatchRoom preserves the state, source snapshots, test contract and proposal history for review.

00:00:39.121 --> 00:00:40.781
The report is simple.

00:00:40.781 --> 00:00:45.127
Shipping should be free at one hundred dollars or more.

00:00:45.127 --> 00:00:49.552
At exactly one hundred, the checkout still charges five.

00:00:49.552 --> 00:00:54.056
In the actual automated case, the triager ran six checks.

00:00:54.056 --> 00:00:55.794
Two assertions failed.

00:00:55.794 --> 00:00:59.982
The failure was reproduced before a fix was proposed.

00:00:59.982 --> 00:01:06.682
The engineer found the cause: a strict greater-than comparison excludes the boundary.

00:01:06.682 --> 00:01:09.598
The authored candidate adds equality.

00:01:09.598 --> 00:01:11.489
One source file changes.

00:01:11.489 --> 00:01:15.036
The baseline and protected tests stay intact.

00:01:15.036 --> 00:01:19.843
The engineer then hands the candidate to a separate verifier.

00:01:19.843 --> 00:01:24.977
The verifier reruns both copies against the same saved contract.

00:01:24.977 --> 00:01:28.186
The baseline still fails two assertions.

00:01:28.186 --> 00:01:33.079
The candidate passes all six checks, with no errors or skips.

00:01:33.079 --> 00:01:37.892
Source and contract hashes identify exactly what was tested.

00:01:37.892 --> 00:01:42.384
The review packet preserves the diff and command output.

00:01:42.384 --> 00:01:45.714
Passing tests does not grant approval.

00:01:45.714 --> 00:01:52.112
This was an automated local report, with no authenticated human reporter.

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:59.473
The installed Switch version omits sender-type metadata required by our review gate.

00:01:59.473 --> 00:02:03.066
PatchRoom stops at awaiting human review.

00:02:03.066 --> 00:02:06.045
No acceptance or merge is claimed.

00:02:06.045 --> 00:02:11.828
Thirty-five workflow and integration tests pass locally and in GitHub Actions.

00:02:11.828 --> 00:02:16.276
Explore the source, real handoffs and verification evidence.

00:02:16.276 --> 00:02:20.131
The public Texmed deployment hosts this walkthrough.

00:02:20.131 --> 00:02:23.244
Agents run locally through Switch Console.

00:02:23.244 --> 00:02:26.506
PatchRoom: three agents, one reviewable fix.
